--TEST--
`Core\Hash::hmac` takes spec § 11's `StrongDigest`, so a legacy `Core\Digest` case does not compile and the diagnostic names the three that do — spec § 11, ADR 0047 § 3
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `StrongDigest` is not a second enum — it is the closed subset of `Digest`,
// stated as ADR 0047 § 3's union of enum-case types. So `Digest::Sha256` is
// one value that both `of` and `hmac` take, and `Digest::Md5` is refused
// here rather than at run time, with the accepted set generated from the
// parameter's own type.
bytes $key = Core\Encoding::fromHex("4a656665");
bytes $mac = Core\Hash::hmac("message", $key, Core\Digest::Md5);
echo Core\Encoding::toHex($mac), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `Core\Digest::Sha256|Core\Digest::Sha384|Core\Digest::Sha512`, found `Core\Digest`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
